<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Document xmlns:p="property" xmlns:r="reflection" Id="OozxXz6rlEyaWUoCJwHXPm" LanguageVersion="2025.7.4" Version="0.128">
  <NugetDependency Id="SIMDywDLwNbQ5UdOPHQxYD" Location="VL.CoreLib" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="Sm17wEPgUJCVB75op3gzPF" Location="VL.Skia" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="CCoTJSCcdlnfZwmjUnPFVB" Location="VL.Mapsui" Version="0.0.0" />
  <!--
    NetTopologySuite is declared HERE, by this document, and that is not the same as VL.Mapsui
    declaring it. VL.Mapsui's own declaration is what lets its node signatures name NTS types; a
    patch that wants to use NTS nodes itself needs its own dependency on it. Measured: without this
    line the node below is "Not found"; with it, it resolves.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="KkbVvAgR3UtmSGnGV4pAoR" Location="NetTopologySuite" Version="2.6.0" />
  <!--
    VL.NetTopologySuite is the package that MAKES geometry; this one draws it. VL.Mapsui's nuspec
    depends on it so that opening this patch does not greet you with red nodes - vvvv does not
    fetch a missing document dependency by itself, it shows it red and offers to install on
    rightclick.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="QVnZMbPyNO4lv6YFocyiqT" Location="VL.NetTopologySuite" Version="0.0.1-alpha" />
  <Patch Id="FJzZkKqVfW12i9kQk6L0hz">
    <Canvas Id="N0E8bKG5vqG1aLaGsfcogC" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pt4eKK7Ag0dikcitT4Vmar">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="T1yChjTcVpcQLJ4rxMEL44">
        <Canvas Id="VxYLn5bECvkjhyGerEE3sc" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VaZNqihOnpwz6dORWEdpu0" Bounds="60,30,620,300" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Styling a layer that holds more than one kind of geometry.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THREE SHAPES, ONE LAYER, ONE STYLE INPUT. A point, a line and a polygon go into the same FeatureLayer - which is what any real dataset looks like - and each needs something different drawn. StyleByGeometry is how you say that: wire a style into Point, Line and Polygon, and each feature is handed the one for its own kind.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE REASON THIS NODE EXISTS. SymbolStyle draws POINTS AND NOTHING ELSE. Not a fainter polygon - none of it. Measured: a polygon covers 14884 pixels under a VectorStyle, 956 under no style at all, and ZERO under a SymbolStyle. Mapsui picks a renderer by the style's runtime type, and it does not help that SymbolStyle derives from VectorStyle. Half a dataset can vanish this way with no error anywhere.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;EVERY MAPPING LIBRARY DOES THIS, in its own words. OpenLayers takes a style function returning styles[geometry.getType()]. Mapbox GL splits circle, line and fill into separate layer types. Leaflet has pointToLayer beside style. A QGIS layer is single-geometry-type with a renderer of its own. Mapsui's mechanism is ThemeStyle, and StyleByGeometry is it with three pins.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TRY: unwire the Polygon pin. The square disappears - and LAYER STATUS names the pin you unplugged. That readout exists for exactly this: FeatureLayer is the only node that sees the features and the style at the same time, and a geometry type with no style draws nothing while Mapsui says nothing about it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TRY: change Shape or Scale. Only the point changes. The line and the polygon are drawn by the VectorStyle and never meet the SymbolStyle at all.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;DO NOT STACK INSTEAD. Sending a VectorStyle and a SymbolStyle to one layer together does draw the polygon - and puts a SECOND circle on every point, because a VectorStyle draws its own 32 pixel marker there too. Measured: Scale 0.6 is 22 pixels across alone and 34 stacked, which is simply the default. That was tried here for an afternoon. Dispatch, do not stack.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;A POINT IS DRAWN AS A CIRCLE, and that is not this package's invention. A point has no size, so something has to stand in for it: Mapsui's own documentation says points are rendered as a circle, Leaflet defaults to a circleMarker, OpenLayers to a circle. To tell a marker from a real shape, ZOOM - a marker keeps its PIXEL size while the ground moves under it. If the size should mean something, buffer the point into a polygon and send that to the Polygon pin; then it is data rather than decoration.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ONE VectorStyle SERVES BOTH the line and the polygon, and which of its pins matter depends on the geometry: Fill Color fills a polygon, Line Color and Line Width stroke a line. That is Mapsui's model rather than a shortcut here.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The shapes come from VL.NetTopologySuite's Read WKT - this package draws geometry, it does not create it. HowTo Draw your own shapes is the one-shape version of this patch; Example GeoJSON on a map reads the same kinds of shape out of a file.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Enabled starts OFF on the tile layer. Opening a document in vvvv runs it, so a map that fetched on open would give you no chance to decline.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Watch Layers Built: it should settle at 1 and stay. A number climbing frame after frame means something rebuilds the layer every frame, and every rebuild starts a fresh round of tile requests. Close vvvv if you see it climb.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="UnaIkq8cPr0a4UZQVn7ji7" Comment="Enabled" Bounds="79,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="false">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="CNYLiTg3BUtmCJlFwHyUjv" Comment="Cache To Disk" Bounds="207,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="true">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="79,340,150,19" Id="JqwwJBWIvaSJq4DTAz8vuN">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="OpenStreetMap" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="Usi9xynIVqJWvRhEvGVOYQ" Name="Enabled" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="ARy89W2GJw4s60rzwfmBsV" Name="Cache" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="VE109xy4WqBycyAwxMeCrD" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="MVGJGduk0mPWJznoGv9YVX" Name="Layers Built" Kind="OutputPin" />
